meta {
  name: Mail
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/mail
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "recipient": "{{playerName}}",
    "subject": "GM API test",
    "text": "Hello from the Bruno collection.",
    "money": 1000
  }
}

docs {
  ## Mail

  Send a GM-stationery mail with text, optional money, and up to 12 item attachments.

  - Method and path: `POST /api/v1/mail`.
  - Path parameters: none.
  - Query parameters: none.
  - Body (JSON, required):
    - `recipient` (string, required, 1-24) — character name; online or offline.
    - `subject` (string, optional, max 64).
    - `text` (string, optional, max 5000).
    - `money` (integer, optional, 0-2147483646) — copper.
    - `items` (array, optional, max 12 entries) — each entry `{"itemId": n, "count": n}` with
      `itemId` minimum 1 and `count` 1-1000. Stacks are split by `MaxStackSize`; after splitting
      the mail may carry at most 12 attachments.
  - Signature headers: `X-GM-Timestamp`, `X-GM-Nonce`, `X-GM-Signature`, plus the write header
    `X-GM-Actor: {{gmActor}}`. All are set by `collection.bru`.
  - Write gate: `GmApi.AllowWrites = 1` (else `403 writes_disabled`).
  - Permissions: `RBAC_PERM_COMMAND_SEND_MAIL` (485) always, plus
    `RBAC_PERM_COMMAND_SEND_ITEMS` (484) when items are attached and
    `RBAC_PERM_COMMAND_SEND_MONEY` (487) when money is sent.
  - Target: the recipient account must be below the actor's security and not the actor's own
    account (`409 cannot_target_self`).
  - Success: `200` with `{"status":"ok"}`. Audit rows: `pending` then `success`.
  - Failure: `400 bad_request`, `invalid_item`, or `too_many_items`; `403 forbidden`;
    `404 target_not_found`; `409 cannot_target_self` or `mailbox_full` (99+ mails);
    `500 mail_failed` or `audit_failed`; `503 world_unavailable`.

  Mail bodies are not stored in the audit arguments.
}
